class:: BlipFB
summary:: Finite Blip kernel with true one-sample normalized phase feedback
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDiff, Classes/BlipDisp, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipKernel, Classes/BlipPM, Classes/BlipPeak, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipSeries, Classes/BlipWidth

description::

BlipFB displaces the shared phase by the previous raw oscillator output times
code::feedback / N::. Division by the effective harmonic count keeps the
maximum retained-partial displacement approximately comparable as bandwidth
changes.

The previous sample is stored before language-side code::mul:: and code::add::
are applied, so post-processing cannot alter the recursive trajectory. The
one-sample state lives inside the native calculation loop and is independent
of server block size. A conservative working range is approximately
code::-2..2:: radians, but finite values are not hard-clipped.

Carrier harmonics are limited before feedback. Recursive phase modulation
creates new, potentially aliased components; dense or noise-like output at
high feedback is not by itself numerical instability. Non-finite state is
cleared immediately.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/SinOscFB::. BlipFB applies the same
one-sample topology to a normalized finite harmonic kernel and compensates for
its highest retained partial.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Carrier frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numharm
Carrier harmonic count, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..2048::
before Nyquist limiting.

argument:: feedback
Audio- or control-rate approximate maximum phase displacement in radians at
the highest partial when the previous raw output is near one.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier. It is not fed back.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset. It is not fed back.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipFB.ar(100, 30, 0.5, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipFB.ar(70, 60, SinOsc.ar(0.1).range(-1, 2), 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipFB.ar(SinOsc.kr(0.1).exprange(100, 1000), LFNoise1.kr(0.5).range(1, 100), MouseX.kr(-0.99, 0.99)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
